			<p><strong>Two days a week</strong> with a public-sector team that inherited a Salesforce org nobody documented. The interesting part is not the org.</p>

			<h2>Reading</h2>
			<p><em>The Timeless Way of Building</em>, slowly and for the second time. <em>Working in Public</em>, which is the only honest book about open source I have found.</p>

			<h2>Not doing</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Conference talks.</strong> Two a year was one too many.</li>
				<li><strong>New clients before November.</strong> Ask anyway — I will tell you when.</li>
				<li><strong>The newsletter every week.</strong> A fortnight is the honest cadence and pretending otherwise made both of us unhappy.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Next</h2>
			<p>Tromsø in February, for the lights. A course on building a Ghost theme from nothing, if enough people say they want it. And at some point, a proper holiday that is not also a shoot.</p>
