<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>The date is the page</h2>
		<p>A now page without a date on it is worse than no now page: a reader cannot tell whether "currently in Amsterdam" was written last week or in 2021, so they assume the worse one and stop trusting the rest of the site with it. The date goes <strong>at the top, beside the title</strong>, not in a footer.</p>

		<h2>Replaced, not appended</h2>
		<p>This is the one page on a site that is allowed to throw its own history away. The previous versions go in a short list at the bottom — <code>im-stream</code> with <code>data-kind="note"</code> — and everything older than two of them is simply gone. A now page that has become a changelog has become a blog with a worse name.</p>

		<h2>"Not doing" is the half that makes it useful</h2>
		<p>Anybody can list what they are working on. The list of what somebody has stopped doing, and why, is the part a reader actually learns something from — and on a page that also says "hire me", it is the part that makes the availability claim believable.</p>
		<div class="im-table-scroll">
		<table>
